# A good share of the students in this lab use Windows. Git for Windows installs with
# core.autocrlf=true by default, which rewrites checked-out text files as CRLF, so:
#   bash scripts/doctor.sh  -> every line reports $'\r': command not found
#   make ...                -> Makefile:N: *** missing separator
# It looks like "every script is broken", but it is only line endings. Pin them to LF
# at the repository level here.
* text=auto eol=lf

# do not normalize line endings in binary files
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
